{"availability":"available","full":"metaplex-foundation/digital-asset-standard-api","name":"digital-asset-standard-api","description":"Open-source specification for interacting with digital assets on Solana.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":66,"forks":24,"created":"2023-10-12T12:09:40Z","updated":"2026-08-27T18:19:58Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://digital-asset-standard-api.typedoc.metaplex.com","topics":[],"demo":"https://playground.open-rpc.org/?url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/metaplex-foundation/digital-asset-standard-api/main/specification/metaplex-das-api.json","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:32.744Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:32.744Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:32.744Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T13:19:32.744Z","stars":66,"forks":24}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The state data of uncompressed NFTs is all stored in on-chain accounts. This is expensive at scale. Compressed NFTs save space by encoding the state data into an on-chain Merkle tree. The detailed account data is not stored on-chain, but in data stores managed by RPC providers. The Metaplex Digital Asset Standard (DAS) API represents a unified interface for interacting with digital assets on Solana, supporting both standard (Token Metadata) and compressed (Bubblegum) assets.","The API defines a set of methods that RPCs implement in order to provide asset data. In the majority of cases, the data is indexed using Metaplex Digital Asset RPC infrastructure."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/metaplex-foundation/digital-asset-standard-api/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4b9b3b4c8055100b32a4b2bc6b982910c97bbe255c280d32d56019c38528724f","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:32.913Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:32.913Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The state data of uncompressed NFTs is all stored in on